From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] irqchip: ingenic: bind the T41 core INTC as two banks

The T41's core interrupt controller at 0x12300000 is the same two-bank
block the JZ4780 and T31 have, one 0x100 register window per CPU core,
each window holding two 32-source banks at 0x20 stride. The vendor
device tree's four `cpu-intc-map` entries are the CPU windows, not four
banks: the T41 IRQ list ends at 63 and QEMU's model exposes exactly two
banks per window (`hw/intc/ingenic-intc.c`).

So the T41 needs no new driver, only the compatible. An earlier
four-bank/0x100 variant put sources 32-63 in the second CPU window and
reported IRQs the peripherals never raise.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/drivers/irqchip/irq-ingenic.c
+++ b/drivers/irqchip/irq-ingenic.c
@@ -159,3 +159,4 @@
 IRQCHIP_DECLARE(jz4775_intc, "ingenic,jz4775-intc", intc_2chip_of_init);
 IRQCHIP_DECLARE(jz4780_intc, "ingenic,jz4780-intc", intc_2chip_of_init);
 IRQCHIP_DECLARE(t31_intc, "ingenic,t31-intc", intc_2chip_of_init);
+IRQCHIP_DECLARE(t41_intc, "ingenic,core-intc", intc_2chip_of_init);
